Currently when handling form data submissions with React Server Components, when the request is not being made with JavaScript, the developer is expected to use `decodeAction` to get the server action function based on the form data to then invoke it.

In our scenario, we need to know the action ID so we can perform additional authentication checks prior to invoking the server action. However, we can't get the action ID for form POST with the current API.

I don't know exactly what the API surface should look like, but we need an implementation similar to `decodeAction` that instead of calling `loadServerReference`, it returns the metadata instead:

```ts
export function decodeActionId<T>(
  body: FormData,
  serverManifest: ServerManifest,
): string | null {
  // We're going to create a new formData object that holds all the fields except
  // the implementation details of the action data.
  const formData = new FormData();

  let actionId: string | null = null;
  const seenActions = new Set<string>();

  // $FlowFixMe[prop-missing]
  body.forEach((value: string | File, key: string) => {
    if (!key.startsWith('$ACTION_')) {
      // $FlowFixMe[incompatible-call]
      formData.append(key, value);
      return;
    }
    // Later actions may override earlier actions if a button is used to
    // override the default form action. However, we don't expect the same
    // action ref field to be sent multiple times in legitimate form data.
    if (key.startsWith('$ACTION_REF_')) {
      if (seenActions.has(key)) {
        return;
      }
      seenActions.add(key);
      const formFieldPrefix = '$ACTION_' + key.slice(12) + ':';
      const metaData = decodeBoundActionMetaData(
        body,
        serverManifest,
        formFieldPrefix,
      );
      actionId = metaData.id;
      return;
    }
    // A simple action with no bound arguments may appear twice in the form data
    // if a button specifies the same action as the default form action. We only
    // load the first one, as they're guaranteed to be identical.
    if (key.startsWith('$ACTION_ID_')) {
      if (seenActions.has(key)) {
        return;
      }
      seenActions.add(key);
      const id = key.slice(11);
      actionId = id;
      return;
    }
  });

  return actionId;
}
```

It's hard to implement this ourselves as well, since many of the functions that the `decodeAction` uses aren't exported.
